--TEST--
a property, class constant or method written without `public`/`protected`/`private` is refused, and there is no implicit `public` to fall back on — ADR 0094 §§ 1, 4
--FILE--
<?mwl
class Account {
    // ADR 0094 § 4: MWL's own grammar accepts this bare property shape, so
    // it is the omission the rule has to catch rather than a parse error.
    int $balance = 0;

    public function constructor(int $opening) {
        $this->balance = $opening;
    }
}
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0122]: a property must declare `public`, `protected` or `private`
  --> case.mwl:5:9
